  "goodToKnow": "Der Radler (die Radlerin) is a cyclist, especially in southern Germany; the standard word is der Radfahrer. Das Radler is a shandy, beer mixed with lemonade, popular in summer. Legend says a Bavarian innkeeper invented it in 1922 for crowds of cyclists, when he ran short of beer; in northern Germany it's called Alsterwasser. Plural: die Radler."
